      <!-- Collision for the walls the stock cafe only ever drew.

           The mesh has a counter, a back room and the upper room's partitions;
           the stock model gives collision to the outer shell and nothing else.
           Ignition's gpu_lidar traces the rendered scene, so on Fortress the
           lidar returns all of it and the robot drives through it; Gazebo
           Classic's ray sensor traces collision, so there it is not there at
           all and the scan disagrees with maps/my_map.yaml.

           These are boxes rather than one mesh collision because dartsim's
           ODE mesh wrapper segfaults building the trimesh: gzserver dies on
           the first physics step inside dart::collision::detail::OdeMesh. They
           are generated by covering the mesh's footprint at the lidar plane
           (z = 0.115) with maximal rectangles, so a diagonal like the counter
           comes out as a short staircase, which is what the 5 cm map raster
           shows anyway. 1.5 m tall: enough to stop the robot and to be seen by
           the lidar, low enough to stay under the mesh ceiling. -->
      <collision name="counter_01">
        <pose>-1.400 6.375 0.9398 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.10 0.55 1.5</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
      </collision>

